      </Band>
      <Band surface="page" id="reading-area">
        <HeadingGroup class="g-section-heading" heading="12 / Reading Area · Aside at end" deck="Close notes avoid each other. Breakouts reserve their rows, and the earliest one stays narrow beside the Aside Block." />
        <ReadingArea>
          <AsideBlock slot="aside" heading="In this notebook" level={3} surface="tint">
            <BodyText><p>A few useful places to begin, collected for the whole article.</p><ul><li><a href="#field-observations">First observations</a></li><li><a href="#field-sketches">From walks to sketches</a></li><li><a href="#field-reflections">What we carried home</a></li></ul><p>Keep a question in mind as you read.</p></BodyText>
          </AsideBlock>
          <BodyText>
            <h3 id="field-observations">An ordinary place, seen together</h3>
            <p>At the start of the walk we each wrote one question. The notebook stayed open, ready for an unexpected answer.</p>
            <Sidenote heading="01 / A question" level={4}><p>What makes a place easy to share? A note can be longer than the sentence that introduced it, and still have a clear place beside the flow.</p></Sidenote>
            <p>Before the bridge, someone pointed out a small sheltered bench.</p>
            <Sidenote heading="02 / Look again" level={4}><p>This note is deliberately close to the first. Its position moves down to leave a readable gap.</p></Sidenote>
            <Figure src={landscape} alt="Layered green hills beside a river" width="wide" caption="An early Breakout keeps Narrow while the Aside Block occupies its row." />
            <p>{runningText}</p><p>{runningText}</p>
            <h3 id="field-sketches">From walks to sketches</h3>
            <p>{runningText}</p>
            <Sidenote heading="03 / A picture note" level={4}><img src={landscape} alt="A tiny study of hills beneath a sun" loading="lazy" /><p>A small drawing records the shape we noticed along the path.</p></Sidenote>
            <Figure src={landscape} alt="A landscape study with a golden sun" width="wide" surface="tint" caption="Wide reaches across the content area. This tint ends with the image, above its caption." />
            <p>{runningText}</p><p>{runningText}</p>
            <Figure src={landscape} alt="An expansive imagined view of green hills" width="full" caption="Full reaches both window edges. The caption still begins at Narrow's reading line." />
            <h3 id="field-reflections">What we carried home</h3>
            <p>{runningText}</p>
            <Sidenote heading="04 / Leave room" level={4}><p>The last note can extend below the final paragraph. The Reading Area contains it so the next band starts beyond its end.</p><p>We left a blank page for the next group to describe the same place in their own words. A shared notebook is most useful when it has room for another perspective.</p></Sidenote>
          </BodyText>
        </ReadingArea>
      </Band>
      <Band surface="tint">
        <HeadingGroup class="g-section-heading" heading="12 / Reading Area · Aside at start" />
        <ReadingArea side="start" stack="after">
          <BodyText><h3>The same path, another view</h3><p>{runningText}</p><Sidenote heading="A different edge" level={4}><p>Logical start and end follow the document's writing direction.</p></Sidenote><p>{runningText}</p><Figure width="bleed-start" src={landscape} alt="An invented study of a hillside" caption="The caption returns to the reading line even with the Aside at start." /><p>{runningText}</p></BodyText>
          <AsideBlock slot="aside" heading="After the story" level={3}><BodyText><p>This block follows the flow in the document and in one column.</p></BodyText></AsideBlock>
        </ReadingArea>
      </Band>
      <Band surface="page">
        <HeadingGroup class="g-section-heading" heading="12 / Reading Area · Centred Narrow" />
